/*
  SettingsExportImport.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0214 · SettingsExportImport (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `SettingsExportImport` resolves (table "SettingsExportImport") lives here with its web
  `t(key, default)` / toast English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without editing
  the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact user-facing copy from the web source
  (features/settings/components/SettingsExportImport.tsx) — the panel title/subtitle, the
  export row, the import dropzone, the parse-error branches, the dry-run preview, the
  applied summary, and the four section labels. The `{{var}}` interpolations are expressed
  natively as `%@` (strings) / `%lld` (counts).

  The remaining keys back the native-only chrome the state list + Apple HIG require: the
  export/import error toast titles + the offline branch (web surfaces these through
  `useMutationToast`), the export button accessibility hint, the toast dismiss, and the
  schema-validator messages (the web `validateSettingsBundle` returns these as raw English
  strings — native routes them through the facade so no English literal lives in the Swift).
*/

